From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brad Barnett <127794626+bdbarnett@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] esp32: a program picks which network interface is the
 default, with nic.ipconfig(default=True).

With Wi-Fi and Ethernet both up, ESP-IDF routes everything off-link by the
interface with the highest route_prio: Wi-Fi's station (100) over Ethernet
(50). A program had no way to move its traffic to Ethernet short of taking
Wi-Fi down. nic.ipconfig(default=True) calls esp_netif_set_default_netif(),
so that interface carries every packet no interface's own subnet claims
while the others stay up and keep their addresses, and
nic.ipconfig("default") says whether it is the default.

ESP-IDF holds that choice until another interface is set or this one is
destroyed (LAN.deinit()), even when its link goes down, so default=False
has nothing to hand back to and is refused: a program moves the default by
setting it on the other interface.

The DNS servers stay as they are. lwIP keeps one list for the whole
stack, written by whichever DHCP lease came last or by
network.ipconfig(dns=...); a server off every link already follows the new
default route. Taking the new default's own DHCP servers would need
CONFIG_ESP_NETIF_SET_DNS_PER_DEFAULT_NETIF on every image, which changes
what network.ipconfig(dns=...) and ifconfig() report, and clears DNS when
the interface has none of its own. A program that wants the interface's own
server sets it with network.ipconfig(dns=...).

The access point no longer restarts its DHCP server when ipconfig() is
given only keys that leave its address alone.
---
diff --git a/docs/library/network.rst b/docs/library/network.rst
index 3da27e39b..51f738e32 100644
--- a/docs/library/network.rst
+++ b/docs/library/network.rst
@@ -125,6 +125,14 @@ parameter should be `id`.
          to be obtained. To check if an address was obtained, use the read-only
          property ``has_dhcp4``.
        * ``gw4`` Get/set the IPv4 default-gateway.
+       * ``default`` (``True``) make this interface the default one: it
+         carries every packet that no interface's own subnet claims, and so
+         the traffic to DNS servers off every link, while the other
+         interfaces stay up. It stays the default until another interface is
+         set, even if its link goes down. The DNS servers don't change; set
+         them with `network.ipconfig` if the new interface needs its own.
+         Reading it says whether this interface is the default. Available on
+         the esp32 port.
        * ``dhcp6`` (``True/False``) obtain a DNS server via stateless DHCPv6.
          Obtaining IP Addresses via DHCPv6 is currently not implemented.
        * ``autoconf6`` (``True/False``) obtain a stateless IPv6 address via
diff --git a/ports/esp32/network_common.c b/ports/esp32/network_common.c
index 3866fef4b..8ce7adf9e 100644
--- a/ports/esp32/network_common.c
+++ b/ports/esp32/network_common.c
@@ -240,6 +240,9 @@ static mp_obj_t esp_ipconfig(size_t n_args, const mp_obj_t *args, mp_map_t *kwar
             case MP_QSTR_gw4: {
                 return netutils_format_ipv4_addr((uint8_t *)&info.gw, NETUTILS_BIG);
             }
+            case MP_QSTR_default: {
+                return mp_obj_new_bool(self->netif != NULL && esp_netif_get_default_netif() == self->netif);
+            }
             default: {
                 mp_raise_ValueError(MP_ERROR_TEXT("unexpected key"));
                 break;
@@ -298,6 +301,20 @@ static mp_obj_t esp_ipconfig(size_t n_args, const mp_obj_t *args, mp_map_t *kwar
                         touched_ip_info = 1;
                         break;
                     }
+                    case MP_QSTR_default: {
+                        // This interface carries every packet that no interface's
+                        // own subnet claims, from now until another interface is
+                        // made the default, whatever route_prio says and whether
+                        // or not its link is up. The DNS servers stay as they are.
+                        if (!mp_obj_is_true(e->value)) {
+                            mp_raise_ValueError(MP_ERROR_TEXT("make another interface the default instead"));
+                        }
+                        if (self->netif == NULL) {
+                            mp_raise_OSError(MP_ENODEV);
+                        }
+                        esp_exceptions(esp_netif_set_default_netif(self->netif));
+                        break;
+                    }
                     default: {
                         mp_raise_ValueError(MP_ERROR_TEXT("unexpected key"));
                         break;
@@ -313,7 +330,7 @@ static mp_obj_t esp_ipconfig(size_t n_args, const mp_obj_t *args, mp_map_t *kwar
                 }
                 esp_exceptions(esp_netif_set_ip_info(self->netif, &info));
             }
-        } else if (self->if_id == ESP_IF_WIFI_AP) {
+        } else if (self->if_id == ESP_IF_WIFI_AP && touched_ip_info) {
             esp_err_t e = esp_netif_dhcps_stop(self->netif);
             if (e != ESP_OK && e != ESP_ERR_ESP_NETIF_DHCP_ALREADY_STOPPED) {
                 esp_exceptions_helper(e);
